Z||000000||SpikeyOrchid||09-09-2001||11:29 PM||||Hi, I'm new to the world of Fiero's (though I have had a love for them for a while now).  But I just bought a 1984 Fiero SE with burnt out wiring.  The people I bought it from said that they had heard of a campain from pontaic that will fix this problem as a recall.  Is this true and is the campain still open?  Also, if anyone has any tips and/or useful info that would help a fiero beginner it would be much apreciated. Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||09-09-2001||11:42 PM||||Verified recalls we know of are all linked in my cave... (Link at top of page.) I'm not sure if the 84 recall will cover cooked wires. <P>Exactly what damage is there and where is it?<P>You may be able to get a replacement engine harness from <A HREF="http://www.kickhill.com/" TARGET=_blank>Kick Hill Farm.</A> He's got nearly every part you could want.<P>changing the harness is more time consuming than dificult. Pretty much only fits one way. not alot of guessing. just take your time, start a one side then move acrosss. that way you plug new things in as you take bad parts off. (You need the battery disconnected while you do this.)<P>Once the new harness is in, have the recall done. This can be a real project and you may have to threaten legal action to get it done. Some dealers are _______ about this and GM isn't much help. Make sure you or or someone you know fully understand the recall documents before you persue this. That way you can tell if they actually did the work when you get it back.||||reg||1
